  "slug": "trees-phylogenetic-d93f",
  "summary": "New resources pair known-truth simulation, a 1000x faster relatedness method and a consolidated ERV reference to make comparative inference more testable and scalable.",
  "synthesis": "The items address distinct problems in comparative sequence analysis, so the shared thread is infrastructure for evaluating and scaling evolutionary inference rather than a common algorithm. OrthoSimulator generates empirically calibrated datasets with known orthogroups and gene trees, supplying ground truth for benchmarking orthology inference. fastpmr is a memory-efficient pairwise mismatch-rate method for relatedness inference that runs over 1000x faster than READv2 and is used to screen the global ancient DNA record. ERV Navigator integrates human endogenous retrovirus annotations, nomenclatures and genomic loci into one phylogenetically informed reference. What is new is the combination of explicit truth or reference frameworks with scalable tooling, which makes comparative inference easier to validate and apply at larger scale.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
